From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:51:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep PPE offload when the NPU refuses flow stats

With flow stats enabled, the offload setup sends the flow stats
request to the NPU and stops when that request fails. An NPU firmware
built without flow counters refuses the request. No flow is then
offloaded, and each offload attempt initializes the NPU PPE again.

A refused request now logs one warning, and offload continues without
flow counters. The PPE then keeps its full SRAM table and does not
send flows through the NPU. The running firmware decides, because the
kernel option and the firmware build can differ.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |    1 
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c |   24 +++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -695,6 +695,7 @@ struct airoha_ppe {
 
 	struct airoha_foe_stats *foe_stats;
 	dma_addr_t foe_stats_dma;
+	bool flow_stats;
 
 	struct dentry *debugfs_dir;
 };
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -44,10 +44,7 @@ static const struct rhashtable_params ai
 
 static int airoha_ppe_get_num_stats_entries(struct airoha_ppe *ppe)
 {
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_FLOW_STATS))
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
-	if (airoha_is_7583(ppe->eth))
+	if (!ppe->flow_stats)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	return PPE_STATS_NUM_ENTRIES;
@@ -157,11 +154,10 @@ static void airoha_ppe_hw_init(struct ai
 		sram_ppe_num_data_entries -= sram_num_stats_entries;
 	sram_ppe_num_data_entries =
 		PPE_RAM_NUM_ENTRIES_SHIFT(sram_ppe_num_data_entries);
-		
-#ifdef CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_FLOW_STATS	
-	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, PSE_FC_CFG, PSE_PORT6_SHARE_DIS, 
-			FIELD_PREP(PSE_PORT6_SHARE_DIS, 0));
-#endif
+
+	if (ppe->flow_stats)
+		airoha_fe_rmw(eth, PSE_FC_CFG, PSE_PORT6_SHARE_DIS,
+			      FIELD_PREP(PSE_PORT6_SHARE_DIS, 0));
 
 	for (i = 0; i < eth->soc->num_ppe; i++) {
 		airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_PPE_TB_BASE(i),
@@ -1538,8 +1534,12 @@ int airoha_ppe_offload_setup(struct airo
 	if (ppe_num_stats_entries > 0) {
 		err = npu->ops.ppe_init_stats(npu, ppe->foe_stats_dma,
 					      ppe_num_stats_entries);
-		if (err)
-			goto error_npu_put;
+		if (err) {
+			dev_warn(eth->dev,
+				 "NPU firmware refused flow stats setup (%d), offload runs without flow counters\n",
+				 err);
+			ppe->flow_stats = false;
+		}
 	}
 
 	airoha_ppe_hw_init(ppe);
@@ -1703,6 +1703,8 @@ int airoha_ppe_init(struct airoha_eth *e
 	ppe->dev.ops.check_tx_skb = arht_ppe_check_tx_skb;
 	ppe->dev.priv = ppe;
 	ppe->eth = eth;
+	ppe->flow_stats = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_FLOW_STATS) &&
+			  !airoha_is_7583(eth);
 
 	ppe_num_entries = airoha_ppe_get_total_num_entries(ppe);
 	foe_size = ppe_num_entries * sizeof(struct airoha_foe_entry);
